{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>In those many days.</b> From the day Moses fled from Egypt in his youth until the birth of Gershom — when Moses was close to eighty years old. For Eliezer was born on the way when he went on the mission of the blessed El to Egypt, and then he was eighty years old." "<b>And the king of Egypt died.</b> That same king who had pursued Moses. Therefore he afterward named his son Eliezer, for then he knew that he had escaped and been saved from Pharaoh's sword." "<b>And they cried out.</b> They cried out from pain of heart over their servitude, as in הֵילִילִי שַׁעַר, זַעֲקִי עִיר (Isaiah 14:31)." "<b>And their cry went up to Elohim from the servitude.</b> Not because of their repentance and prayer, but as one zealous against the cruelty of the taskmasters, as it says: וְגַם רָאִיתִי אֶת הַלַּחַץ (Exodus 3:9)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:07.422074382Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}